End to end
==========

These run against a deployed daemon, not against the package. The unit tests stub
obol, systemd and Luna; these do not, which is the point.

    bash tests/e2e/on-the-controller.sh

On the controller itself. Needs a shell there: it reads the store, restarts the
unit and checks the rule files on disk as well as the API.

    python3 tests/e2e/over-http.py <controller>

From anywhere that can reach the two ports. Covers the API, the pass-through, the
hot swap, the queue, the bits and the replication documents, and nothing that
needs a shell.

Both leave the store as they found it. Neither is run by pytest: they need a
daemon and a Luna, and a test that quietly passes when there is no daemon is
worse than no test.
